<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The thaw, and the only lasting thing a frost bomb does.

       The hard freeze is a stun, applied in code, and it is over in three seconds. This is what
       happens afterwards: a target that comes out of the cloud slow, clumsy, and worth shooting
       at, getting better every second whether anyone helps them or not.

       Severity is the thaw clock. It lands at the fraction of the blast the target caught and
       sheds at 100/day, which is ten seconds from a centre hit to nothing at all. Those units
       look absurd - severity per *day* on an effect measured in seconds - but severityPerDay is
       the only shedding comp the game has, and 100 is simply what ten seconds costs in it.

       Deliberately not isBad. It is not an injury, nothing treats it, and a doctor being told
       to go and tend somebody who will be fine before they arrive is a bug. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>AG_Frostbound</defName>
    <label>frostbound</label>
    <description>This person has been caught in a cryogenic burst. Muscle and joint fluid are still near freezing: they move slowly and cannot grip properly.\n\nIt passes on its own within seconds. Nothing needs to be done about it.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.62, 0.82, 0.95)</defaultLabelColor>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-100</severityPerDay>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <!-- Clipped by the edge of the cloud. Cold hands, nothing more. -->
      <li>
        <label>chilled</label>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.15</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.15</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.35</minSeverity>
        <label>rimed</label>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.45</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.40</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <!-- Straight out of the cloud. Movement is most of the way gone and the hands are useless,
           but this is the stage that lasts the least time - it sheds into 'rimed' in about three
           seconds. Never a full stop: the stun already did that, and stacking a zero capacity on
           top of it would leave a pawn frozen well after the ice has visibly gone. -->
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.70</minSeverity>
        <label>frozen through</label>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.75</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.70</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
